From: GeekezBrowser <build@geekez.net>
Date: 2026-01-01
Subject: [PATCH 002] Canvas noise injection - seed-based deterministic

Adds deterministic, seed-based pixel noise to canvas readback operations.

Key improvements over JS injection:
- Noise is applied at C++ level (undetectable via JS property inspection)
- Property descriptors remain completely native
- Seed-based: same seed = same fingerprint (persistent across page reloads)
- Noise is imperceptible visually but changes fingerprint hash

Controlled via --canvas-noise-seed=<uint32> command line flag.
Set to 0 to disable (passthrough to original implementation).

Detection tests this bypasses:
- getImageData() hook detection
- toDataURL() property descriptor checks
- toString() native code verification
